# HospitalOS scheduled jobs — crontab for the production server
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The app ships 13 cron ROUTES but nothing was ever calling them, so none of the
# scheduled work was running: no appointment reminders, no SLA checks, no queued
# email delivery, no scheduled MIS report delivery.
#
# Install with:   bash aws/cron/install-cron.sh
# Inspect with:   crontab -l
# Logs:           /home/ubuntu/hospitalos/logs/cron.log
#
# Every endpoint is called with GET — most of these routes only implement GET
# (they answer 405 to POST), which is also how Vercel Cron invokes them.
#
# Requires two shell variables, set by the installer from the app's .env:
#   APP_URL       e.g. http://localhost:3000   (loopback: no public round trip)
#   CRON_SECRET   must match CRON_SECRET in .env, or every call gets 401
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
CRON_SECRET=__CRON_SECRET__
LOG=/home/ubuntu/hospitalos/logs/cron.log

# --- Frequent queues ---------------------------------------------------------
# Outbound email queue. Drains PENDING jobs in batches with a retry cap.
*/2 * * * * curl -fsS -m 60 -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" "$APP_URL/api/cron/email-dispatch" >> $LOG 2>&1

# Scheduled broadcasts — sends the ones staff queued for a future time.
*/5 * * * * curl -fsS -m 60 -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" "$APP_URL/api/cron/broadcast-dispatch" >> $LOG 2>&1

# TPA / claim SLA breaches — raises internal alerts only.
*/15 * * * * curl -fsS -m 120 -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" "$APP_URL/api/cron/sla-check" >> $LOG 2>&1

# Nursing assessment alerts — internal alerts for overdue assessments.
*/30 * * * * curl -fsS -m 120 -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" "$APP_URL/api/cron/assessment-alerts" >> $LOG 2>&1

# --- Hourly ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scheduled MIS report delivery. Without this, the "Schedule" button on a report
# stores a schedule that never fires.
5 * * * * curl -fsS -m 300 -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" "$APP_URL/api/cron/mis-scheduled-delivery" >> $LOG 2>&1

# --- Daily -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Patient WhatsApp reminders for TOMORROW's appointments only. Guarded by
# reminder24Sent, so a patient is never messaged twice and there is no backlog
# to flush on first run.
0 18 * * * curl -fsS -m 300 -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" "$APP_URL/api/cron/appointment-reminders" >> $LOG 2>&1

# Budget threshold alerts — internal.
0 0 * * * curl -fsS -m 300 -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" "$APP_URL/api/cron/budget-alerts" >> $LOG 2>&1

# MIS pre-aggregation, then cleanup of old report jobs/files.
30 2 * * * curl -fsS -m 900 -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" "$APP_URL/api/cron/mis-rollup" >> $LOG 2>&1
0 2 * * *  curl -fsS -m 300 -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" "$APP_URL/api/cron/mis-cleanup" >> $LOG 2>&1

# Asset maintenance / warranty reminders — in-app notification to admins.
0 3 * * * curl -fsS -m 300 -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" "$APP_URL/api/cron/asset-maintenance-reminders" >> $LOG 2>&1

# --- Inpatient operations ----------------------------------------------------
# These three live under /api/ipd/ rather than /api/cron/, which is why the
# original sweep of "the 13 cron routes" missed them. They are real, implemented
# endpoints that nothing was calling.

# Bed cleaning sweep. Returns beds left in "Cleaning" past the 24h backstop to
# the available pool, across every active organization. Without this the sweep
# only ever ran when a member of staff happened to open an IPD page.
0 * * * * curl -fsS -m 120 -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" "$APP_URL/api/ipd/bed-cleaning-sla" >> $LOG 2>&1

# Deposit alerts. Warns finance and the IPD manager while an inpatient's advance
# is running out, rather than at discharge when it is too late to ask.
0 */4 * * * curl -fsS -m 120 -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" "$APP_URL/api/ipd/deposit-alerts" >> $LOG 2>&1

# Interim billing. Flags long-staying admissions that are due an interim bill and
# tells the billing team. It deliberately does not raise the bill itself —
# generating a financial document needs an accountable user.
30 6 * * * curl -fsS -m 300 -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" "$APP_URL/api/ipd/interim-billing" >> $LOG 2>&1

# Medication chart top-up. The MAR is filled to a rolling three-day horizon and
# opening an eMAR already rolls it forward, so this is the safety net for a ward
# that has not been opened over a long weekend — it must never run dry.
15 2 * * * curl -fsS -m 300 -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" "$APP_URL/api/ipd/mar-topup" >> $LOG 2>&1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DELIBERATELY NOT SCHEDULED — each needs a decision, not a default:
#
#   /api/ipd/daily-accrual
#       Returns early by design: "Auto-accrual disabled. Room/nursing charges
#       are added manually." Scheduling it would do nothing. If a site ever
#       wants automatic room/nursing accrual, re-enable the route first.
#
#   /api/cron/depreciation
#       Posts monthly depreciation JOURNAL ENTRIES to the general ledger.
#       Turning it on writes to the books, and if it has never run there may be
#       catch-up periods. Finance should agree the first period before enabling:
#           0 0 1 * *   (1st of each month)
#
#   /api/cron/pill-reminders
#       Fires only for reminders whose schedule_times contains the exact current
#       HH:MM, so it must run EVERY MINUTE or most doses are missed. It also
#       resolves the tenant from a user session, which a cron does not have —
#       confirm it actually sends for a test patient before scheduling:
#           * * * * *   (every minute)
#
#   /api/cron/mis-jobs
#       Retired. It answers 410 Gone on purpose, to tell a scheduler to stop
#       calling it. Do not schedule.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
